<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.3.4: Finding the Solutions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02130</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.3.4: Finding the Solutions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f4560f1d-0b55-4f1f-8e0a-02cdb4bc3304</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>Use what you have learned in the lesson to solve the following quadratic equations.</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(5m^2= 80\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the solution to the equation.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(m=4\) and \(m=-4\)</para>
    <para>\(5m^2=80\)</para>
    <para> \(\frac{5m^2}{5}=\frac{80}{5}\)</para>
    <para> \(m^2=16\)</para>
    <para> \(m=\pm \sqrt{16}\)</para>
    <para> \(m=4\) and \(m=-4\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\((m−6)^2=100\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the solution to the equation.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(m=16\) and \(m=-4\)</para>
    <para>\((m−6)^2=100\)</para>
    <para>\((m−6)=\pm \sqrt{100}\)</para>
    <para>\(m−6=10\;\;\;\;m−6=-10\)</para>
    <para>\(m =16\) and \(m =-4\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(\frac{2}{3}y^2−8=−2\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the solution to the equation.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(y=3\) and \(y=-3\)</para>
    <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}\frac23y^2-8&amp;=&amp;-2\\\frac23y^2&amp;=&amp;6\\\frac32\left(\frac23y^2\right)&amp;=&amp;\frac32\left(6\right)\\y^2&amp;=&amp;9\\y&amp;=&amp;\pm\sqrt9\end{array}\)\(\;\;\;\;\;\;y=3\) and \(y=-3\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(\frac{1}{6}(x+3)^2−8=16\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the solution to the equation.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(x=9\) and \(x=-15\)</para>
    <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}\frac16\left(x+3\right)^2-8&amp;=&amp;16\\\frac16\left(x+3\right)^2&amp;=&amp;24\\\left(x+3\right)^2&amp;=&amp;144\\\left(x+3\right)&amp;=&amp;\pm\sqrt{144}\end{array}\)
      \(\;\;\;\;\;\;\;x+3=12\;\;\;\;\;\;x+3=-12\)
      \(\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;\;x=9\) and \(x=-15\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
